R4.3-R2.6.22-F2: reuse the persistent input surface across video encoders

EncoderImpl.SurfaceInput parks its persistent input surface after MediaCodec.release() instead of
releasing it, and the next video encoder takes a parked surface before creating a new one. On
Android 13 (Codec2) this frees the C2OMXNode (and its 20 ms polling thread) that a codec released
while only configured leaves behind: re-associating the same persistent surface with another codec
replaces the GraphicBufferSource component that kept the old node alive. Validated on SM-A326B in
the R2.6.22-F2 harness; see ../PATCHES.md.

